---
import SectionLayout from "../../layouts/SectionLayout.astro";

import Title from "../Title.astro";
import Description from "../Description.astro";
import { cn } from "../../utils/cn";

// Navigation items for the whitepaper
const navItems = [
  { id: "overview", label: "1. Executive Overview" },
  { id: "how-it-works", label: "2. How It Works" },
  { id: "utility", label: "3. Utility & Governance" },
  { id: "contract", label: "4. Smart Contract Architecture" },
  { id: "ecosystem", label: "5. Ecosystem & Liquidity" },
  { id: "tokenomics", label: "6. Tokenomics" },
  { id: "transparency", label: "7. Transparency & Reporting" },
  { id: "roadmap", label: "8. Governance & Roadmap" },
  { id: "security", label: "9. Security & Risk Mitigation" },
  { id: "team", label: "10. Team" },
  { id: "legal", label: "11. Legal Notice" },
];

const contentData = [
  {
    id: "overview",
    title: "1. Executive Overview",
    text: `VETRA (VTR) is a utility and governance token deployed on the Polygon network. It is not a stablecoin and carries no fixed parity with any currency.

VTR is built on an open, fully auditable on-chain infrastructure: a verified smart contract, a public liquidity pool on Uniswap V3, and open-market trading. The protocol focuses on three things that exist today — efficient transfers, low fees, and verifiable transparency.

Key Metrics (September 2026):
- Token: VTR (ERC-20)
- Total Supply: 30,000,000 VTR
- Maximum Supply (cap): 1,000,000,000 VTR
- Blockchain: Polygon Mainnet (Chain ID 137)
- Transfer Tax: 0%
- Primary Liquidity: Uniswap V3 — VTR/USDC pool
- Contract: verified and publicly auditable on PolygonScan`,
  },
  {
    id: "how-it-works",
    title: "2. How It Works",
    text: `VTR is a standard ERC-20 token. There is no intermediary, no custodian and no reserve account involved in its operation.

Circulation
Transfers happen directly between wallets on Polygon. There is no transfer tax, no per-transaction limit, no per-wallet limit and no cooldown — by design, so the token circulates freely.

Fee Structure
Sending VTR costs only the network gas fee of the Polygon blockchain. The protocol itself charges nothing.

Verification
Every parameter described in this document — supply, cap, balances and transfers — can be independently verified by anyone on PolygonScan. No trust in the team is required to confirm the facts.`,
  },
  {
    id: "utility",
    title: "3. Utility & Governance",
    text: `What VTR Is
VTR is the utility and governance token of the VETRA protocol. Its functions are technical and operational, not promotional.

Governance
The protocol is administered through distinct on-chain roles, each with limited scope:
- MINTER — controls issuance, always within the hard cap
- BURNER — can permanently remove tokens from circulation
- PAUSER — can pause the contract in an emergency
- UPGRADER — authorizes contract upgrades
This separation means no single action requires — or grants — unchecked authority.

Utility Today
- Free circulation: transfer, receive and integrate VTR without friction
- Liquidity provision: VTR is one side of the live VTR/USDC pool on Uniswap V3
- Governance participation: token holders are the constituency the protocol answers to
- Verifiability: every supply and transfer event is public and permanent

What VTR Is Not
VTR is not a stablecoin, is not pegged to any fiat currency, and is not backed by a fixed reserve. Its market value is discovered openly on the secondary market.`,
  },
  {
    id: "contract",
    title: "4. Smart Contract Architecture",
    text: `Deployed on Polygon Mainnet (Chain ID 137):

- Token contract (proxy): 0xAA27bd271B01dd20CcFA079800616335416c95Fd
- Standard: ERC-20 with upgradeable proxy (UUPS / ERC-1967)
- Source code: verified and readable on PolygonScan
- Compiler: Solidity 0.8.x, optimizer enabled

Design Choices
- Upgradeable (UUPS): allows the protocol to evolve without changing the token address, holder balances or integrations. The same architecture is used by the largest tokens in the market.
- Hard cap: issuance can never exceed 1,000,000,000 VTR.
- Role-based access control: administrative actions are split across four distinct roles.
- Pausable: a dedicated role can halt transfers in a verified emergency.
- No hidden fees: the contract applies no transfer tax and no blacklist.

Transparency
Anyone can read the contract, verify the supply, and audit every administrative action directly on the blockchain.`,
  },
  {
    id: "ecosystem",
    title: "5. Ecosystem & Liquidity",
    text: `Primary Liquidity Pool
VETRA's primary liquidity pool operates on Uniswap V3 (Polygon):
- Pair: VTR / USDC | Fee Tier: 0.05%
- Pool: 0x5484C717168175cFFDd77678ecAC3A38e76c4e2B
- Protocol-owned liquidity (POL) — the project holds its own liquidity position

Liquidity Strategy
Liquidity is concentrated in overlapping price ranges, ensuring continuous trading and reducing slippage for users. Deepening liquidity is an ongoing operational focus.

Where VTR Trades
- Uniswap V3 (on-chain, permissionless)
- KuCoin (centralized exchange listing)
- Aggregators and trackers: GeckoTerminal, CoinGecko, CoinMarketCap, DexScreener
- Contract verification: PolygonScan

Note
Liquidity depth is publicly visible. We do not use treasury funds to defend or manipulate the market price; price discovery is left to the open market.`,
  },
  {
    id: "tokenomics",
    title: "6. Tokenomics",
    text: `Supply
- Total supply: 30,000,000 VTR
- Hard cap (on-chain): 1,000,000,000 VTR
- No issuance is scheduled. Any future issuance would be a deliberate, publicly communicated decision and could never exceed the cap.

Distribution (approximate)
- Treasury: held by the project's administrative wallet
- Operations: liquidity provision, integrations and development
- Community: public market participants and VTR holders

Policy
Supply changes emit on-chain events and are publicly verifiable. There is no hidden mint, no rebase and no algorithmic expansion mechanism.`,
  },
  {
    id: "transparency",
    title: "7. Transparency & Reporting",
    text: `Verification Without Intermediaries
Every claim made in this document is verifiable on-chain. No custodian, auditor or third party needs to be trusted:
• Supply and cap — readable directly from the contract
• Transfers — recorded permanently on Polygon
• Administrative actions — emitted as events and publicly visible
• Source code — verified on PolygonScan

Principle
If a statement cannot be verified by anyone with a block explorer, it is not claimed here.

Corrections
Earlier documentation described a different model (a collateralized structure with an external custody partner). That arrangement was discontinued by the partner and is no longer in place. This document supersedes all previous versions.`,
  },
  {
    id: "roadmap",
    title: "8. Governance & Roadmap",
    text: `Completed:
✅ Polygon mainnet deployment
✅ UUPS proxy with verified implementation
✅ Migration to utility-token model (contract V3)
✅ Removal of legacy reserve parameters and transfer limits
✅ Fixed supply cap (1,000,000,000 VTR) implemented on-chain
✅ Role-based governance (Admin, Minter, Burner, Pauser, Upgrader)
✅ Contract verified on PolygonScan
✅ Open OTC exchange for VTR (quote, payment and on-chain delivery)

Next Phase (operations):
🔲 Hardware-wallet custody with timelock delay
🔲 Public transparency dashboard
🔲 Deeper liquidity and market integrations

We only describe as available what can be used today. Anything that cannot be verified on-chain is not claimed here.`,
  },
  {
    id: "security",
    title: "9. Security & Risk Mitigation",
    text: `Protocol Security Layers
1. Supply: hard on-chain cap — issuance can never exceed it
2. Technical: UUPS upgradeability with role-based access control
3. Emergency: pausable mechanism for critical situations
4. Monitoring: real-time event monitoring and operational alerts
5. Custody: migration to hardware-wallet custody with timelock delay

Risk Factors
• Smart contract risk: source code verified and auditable on PolygonScan
• Market risk: price is discovered organically; liquidity depth may be limited
• Regulatory risk: token utility and applicable rules vary by jurisdiction
• Technology risk: the protocol depends on the Polygon network

No statement in this document should be read as a guarantee of price, yield or future performance.`,
  },
  {
    id: "team",
    title: "10. Team",
    text: `The protocol is developed by a small, accountable team that operates in public:

- Pedro Fares Ramos — Founder & CEO. Leads strategy, protocol development and partnerships.
- Rosemberg Alves Nascimento — Co-Founder. Leads global partnerships and commercial development.

We publish what we build. Our commitment is to keep public communication limited to what is verifiable on-chain.`,
  },
  {
    id: "legal",
    title: "11. Legal Notice",
    text: `This document is provided for informational purposes only. It does not constitute financial, investment, legal or tax advice, nor an offer or solicitation to buy or sell any asset.

VTR is a utility and governance token. It is not a security, share, bond, collective investment scheme or stablecoin, and it does not grant any ownership or profit-sharing rights in any entity.

Digital assets involve significant risk, including total loss of value. Market prices are volatile and determined by open-market supply and demand. Nothing in this document should be interpreted as a promise of price, return or future functionality.

Statements about items "in development" describe ongoing research objectives. They are not commitments, and no timeline should be inferred.

Users are responsible for complying with the laws applicable in their jurisdiction.`,
  },
];

// Seções para o script (versão achatada com \n\n)
const contentDataFlat = contentData.map((s) => ({
  id: s.id,
  title: s.title,
  text: s.text.replace(/\n/g, "\\n"),
}));
---

<SectionLayout id="whitepaper-content" class="relative overflow-hidden">
  <div class="relative z-10 max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="flex flex-col lg:flex-row gap-8 lg:gap-12">
      <!-- Navegação lateral -->
      <aside class="lg:w-[280px] shrink-0">
        <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-24">
          <nav class="flex flex-row lg:flex-col gap-2 overflow-x-auto lg:overflow-x-visible pb-2 lg:pb-0">
            {
              navItems.map((item) => (
                <a
                  href={`#${item.id}`}
                  data-nav={item.id}
                  class="whitepaper-nav whitespace-nowrap lg:whitespace-normal text-left px-4 py-2.5 rounded-lg text-[14px] leading-[20px] text-text-grey hover:text-text-secondary hover:bg-white/[0.04] transition-colors"
                >
                  {item.label}
                </a>
              ))
            }
          </nav>
        </div>
      </aside>

      <!-- Conteúdo -->
      <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
        <div id="whitepaper-sections" class="flex flex-col gap-12">
          {
            contentData.map((section) => (
              <section id={section.id} data-section={section.id} class="scroll-mt-28">
                <Title
                  text={section.title}
                  className={cn(
                    "text-text-secondary text-[24px] leading-[32px] max-sm:text-[20px] max-sm:leading-[28px] mb-4"
                  )}
                />
                <Description
                  text={section.text}
                  className="whitespace-pre-line text-text-grey text-[16px] leading-[26px]"
                />
              </section>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script is:inline define:vars={{ contentDataFlat }}>
    (() => {
      const data = contentDataFlat;

      // Scroll suave ao clicar na navegação
      document.querySelectorAll(".whitepaper-nav").forEach((link) => {
        link.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
          e.preventDefault();
          const id = link.getAttribute("data-nav");
          const target = document.getElementById(id);
          if (target) {
            target.scrollIntoView({ behavior: "smooth", block: "start" });
            history.replaceState(null, "", `#${id}`);
          }
        });
      });

      // Destaque da seção ativa durante o scroll
      const sections = document.querySelectorAll("[data-section]");
      const navLinks = document.querySelectorAll(".whitepaper-nav");

      const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
        (entries) => {
          entries.forEach((entry) => {
            if (entry.isIntersecting) {
              const id = entry.target.getAttribute("data-section");
              navLinks.forEach((l) => {
                const active = l.getAttribute("data-nav") === id;
                l.classList.toggle("bg-white/[0.06]", active);
                l.classList.toggle("text-text-secondary", active);
              });
            }
          });
        },
        { rootMargin: "-20% 0px -70% 0px", threshold: 0 }
      );

      sections.forEach((s) => observer.observe(s));
    })();
  </script>
</SectionLayout>
